<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>Personal BaaS</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/admin/static/css/admin.css" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/admin/static/css/landing.css" />
</head>
<body class="landing-page">
  <main class="landing-hero">
    <span class="landing-badge">Self-hosted</span>
    <h1>Personal BaaS</h1>
    <p class="landing-tagline">
      Point it at a Postgres schema. Get back a secure REST API, auth, storage, serverless
      functions, and an admin console — running entirely on your own infrastructure.
    </p>
    <div class="landing-cta-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/admin/login">Open Admin Console →</a>
      <a class="btn btn-outline btn-lg" href="/security-report">View Security Report</a>
    </div>

    <div class="landing-features">
      <div class="landing-feature">
        <h3>Instant REST APIs</h3>
        <p>PostgREST turns tables, views, and functions into a live API — no boilerplate.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="landing-feature">
        <h3>Auth, JWTs & MFA</h3>
        <p>Email/password signup and login, project-scoped JWTs, and optional TOTP two-factor with backup codes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="landing-feature">
        <h3>Row-level security</h3>
        <p>Access control lives in Postgres policies, not application code.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="landing-feature">
        <h3>Rate limiting</h3>
        <p>Per-route throttling protects your API from abuse out of the box.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="landing-feature">
        <h3>Object storage</h3>
        <p>Upload, download, and manage files per user or per bucket.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="landing-feature">
        <h3>Static hosting</h3>
        <p>Deploy a static site or frontend build alongside your API.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="landing-feature">
        <h3>Serverless functions</h3>
        <p>Run project-scoped JS/TS in an isolated worker — no separate deploy pipeline.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="landing-feature">
        <h3>Scheduler</h3>
        <p>Cron-style jobs trigger functions on a schedule — no external cron needed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="landing-feature">
        <h3>Secrets vault</h3>
        <p>Encrypted, write-only secrets for functions and integrations — never re-displayed in plaintext.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="landing-feature">
        <h3>Transactional email</h3>
        <p>Send email straight from your backend without wiring up a third-party SaaS.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="landing-feature">
        <h3>On-demand PDFs</h3>
        <p>Generate PDFs from functions for invoices, reports, and receipts.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="landing-feature">
        <h3>SQL editor & DB explorer</h3>
        <p>Browse schemas and run queries straight from the browser.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="landing-feature">
        <h3>API Explorer</h3>
        <p>Discover and test every live endpoint without leaving the console.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="landing-feature">
        <h3>Multi-project isolation</h3>
        <p>Run several isolated projects on one Postgres instance — separate schemas, roles, and users.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="landing-feature">
        <h3>Audit log</h3>
        <p>Every operator action is recorded — who did what, and when.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <footer class="landing-footer">
    Personal BaaS — self-hosted Backend-as-a-Service · <a href="/security-report">Security</a>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
